  "description": "XIDPOR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H78 Dy4 N4 O21,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.453-4.105 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.84-126.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C89H90Dy4N4O24. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
